### Method 1: Iterative Loop (The most fundamental approach)

This is the most straightforward and fundamental way to calculate the length. It iterates through the string character by character until it encounters the null terminator (`\0`).

```c
#include <stddef.h> // Required for size_t, though often implicitly included

/**
 * @brief Calculates the length of a null-terminated string without using strlen.
 *
 * @param str The string to measure.
 * @return The length of the string (number of characters before the null terminator).
 */
size_t custom_strlen(const char *str) {
    if (str == NULL) {
        return 0; // Handle the case where the input pointer is NULL
    }

    size_t length = 0;
    // Loop until the current character pointed to by 'str' is the null terminator ('\0')
    while (str[length] != '\0') {
        length++;
    }

    return length;
}

